  "_comment": "Shared runtime/image test vectors: cua-fleet (tests/image_variants.rs) and cua-sandbox (tests/test_fleet_image_variants.py) both run them. An image is a containerDisk when its manifest/config shows /disk/disk.img or a trycua containerDisk media type, else a rootfs; a readable manifest always beats the tag. A case with `refused` is a macOS image: classifying it is a typed Unsupported error whose message contains that text. `fallbacks`: the runtime chosen from the reference alone when the manifest cannot be read and no runtime is given (a tag starting with docker- or containing -docker- is gvisor, anything else kubevirt).",
